03:13:53.010 --> 03:13:54.610
Nenita Camposano: Yes, Your Honor. Typically

03:13:54.610 --> 03:13:55.890
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: magkano yun in a month?

03:13:56.850 --> 03:14:00.690
Nenita Camposano: Hindi ko na siya ma-recall pero way below.

03:14:01.450 --> 03:14:03.490
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: More or less 10 million, 20 million,

03:14:03.730 --> 03:14:04.910
Nenita Camposano: 5

03:14:04.910 --> 03:14:06.510
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: million, more or less.

03:14:08.590 --> 03:14:13.150
Nenita Camposano: Yung total for the month? For the month lang. Mga hundreds lang siguro yun. 100

03:14:13.150 --> 03:14:13.690
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: million?

03:14:14.210 --> 03:14:15.530
Nenita Camposano: No, 100,000.

03:14:16.030 --> 03:14:19.930
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So 100,000 is typical. encashment for payroll.

03:14:20.130 --> 03:14:22.550
Nenita Camposano: 100,000 to 100,000. Mga ganoon lamang. 100

03:14:22.550 --> 03:14:26.430
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: ,000. And then, rinig ko kanina na galing kayo sa ibang branch.

03:14:26.690 --> 03:14:27.150
Nenita Camposano: Yes.

03:14:27.870 --> 03:14:30.910
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: May experience rin kayo sa ibang government agencies?

03:14:31.470 --> 03:14:32.030
Nenita Camposano: Meron po.

03:14:32.290 --> 03:14:39.770
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Meron din ba kayong mga experience na ganito kalaking amount ang ini-encash ng isang government agency?

03:14:41.710 --> 03:14:49.150
Nenita Camposano: As to amount, hindi ko na rin po siya matanda. Pero ang alam ko po, malaki rin po yung i-encash ng ibang government agents.

03:14:49.390 --> 03:14:55.490
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Ganito to a tune of 37.5 million. Around that vicinity?

03:14:56.150 --> 03:14:57.630
Nenita Camposano: More or less siguro. More

03:14:57.630 --> 03:15:03.610
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: or less. So meron ganyan kayong na-experience pag i-encash sa ibang branch?

03:15:04.730 --> 03:15:05.290
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir.

03:15:05.390 --> 03:15:20.010
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Tama po ba? And then, balik tayo dito sa DepEd. Doon sa pag-a-advise sa inyo tuwing mag-e-encash, gaano kaaga dapat mag-advise sa inyo bago mag-encash?

03:15:21.870 --> 03:15:22.390
Nenita Camposano: Kung

03:15:22.390 --> 03:15:23.290
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: kailangan ng cash.

03:15:23.750 --> 03:15:35.230
Nenita Camposano: Usually dapat morning masabihan na po kami. Kasi siguro mga 12 o'clock magka-cut off na rin po yung cash center namin para i-request din po yun. So within

03:15:35.230 --> 03:15:37.630
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: 24 hours dapat ma-advise na kayo?

03:15:41.010 --> 03:15:44.090
Nenita Camposano: Hindi naman siya 24 hours, sir. Less

03:15:44.090 --> 03:15:45.450
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: than 24 hours? Pag

03:15:45.450 --> 03:15:45.910
Nenita Camposano: nasabihan

03:15:45.910 --> 03:15:48.170
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: kayo, mapapadala nyo ka agad doon yung

03:15:48.170 --> 03:15:48.870
Nenita Camposano: cash na ganun

03:15:48.870 --> 03:15:49.230
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: kalaki?

03:15:49.410 --> 03:16:00.070
Nenita Camposano: Yes. May katao po kasi ang cash center namin, siguro ma around 12 o'clock. So pagka mas later lang 12 o'clock, hindi pa rin namin masagot na ma-deliver sa amin yung the following day.

03:16:00.770 --> 03:16:04.570
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Itong branch ninyo, particularly para sa DepEd, tama po ba?

03:16:04.750 --> 03:16:05.670
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir. Sa

03:16:05.670 --> 03:16:19.350
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: inyong pagkaalam sa mga past mga DepEd officials, past secretaries, Meron na bang na-encash na ganito hukalaki? Sa inyong pagkaalam, kasi alam ko two years pa lang kayo doon, pero sa inyong mga pag-uusap sa inyong staff?

03:16:21.050 --> 03:16:23.050
Nenita Camposano: Hindi namin na pag-uusapan, sir.

03:16:23.230 --> 03:16:23.710
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Ang

03:16:23.710 --> 03:16:28.190
Nenita Camposano: alam ko lang po is yung stint ko sa DepEd. Hindi

03:16:28.190 --> 03:16:36.010
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: nyo na pag-uusapan sa mga subordinates nyo kung may mga ganitong encashment na malalaki? May mga ganun bang pag-uusap kayo?

03:16:36.930 --> 03:16:38.250
Nenita Camposano: Wala po. Thank

03:16:38.250 --> 03:16:39.010
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: you, Mr. President.

03:16:39.740 --> 03:16:51.860
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senate President Gachalian. Next to make his interjections would be Senator Rafi Tulfo. You're recognized, sir. You may proceed when you're ready. You have two minutes, sir.

03:17:00.340 --> 03:17:16.440
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Madam Witness, ayon sa COA Circular 2015-01, pagdating sa disbursement ng confidential file, ang authorized lang dapat talaga yung head ng agency or yung designated person.

03:17:17.320 --> 03:17:17.840
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: ng

03:17:17.840 --> 03:17:26.090
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: agency na yon. You agree? And in this case, ang SDO is Edward Fajarda. Alam na natin, kanina pa natin pag-usapan. Correct?

03:17:26.370 --> 03:17:26.890
Nenita Camposano: Yes.

03:17:27.230 --> 03:17:37.750
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Now, anong mga dokumentong sinamiti sa land bank, the land bank, para magpapatunay na in fact talagang si Edward Fajarda ang designated SDO?

03:17:38.930 --> 03:17:41.090
Nenita Camposano: Wala po. Wala? Wala po.

03:17:41.610 --> 03:17:55.520
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Anong sinabing wala? So, Walang dokumentong isinumite na dinedesignate si Fajarda ng head ng agency na yan para sabihin ito ang SDO. Ito yung maging katransaksyon nyo? Wala? Wala. Laway lang?

03:17:58.670 --> 03:18:05.250
Nenita Camposano: Nagpunta po doon si Mr. Fajarda na siya yung payee at nagpresent po siya ng identification. Of

03:18:05.250 --> 03:18:12.330
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: course, pero dapat meron siyang dokumentong pinipresent na siya ang dinedesignate ng head ng agency na yun bilang SDO. Right?

03:18:13.090 --> 03:18:14.510
Nenita Camposano: Wala po silang naipresent

03:18:14.510 --> 03:18:23.700
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: sa amin. And then you honor it? Face value? Nagpakita lang siya ng dokumento? Ako si Fajarda at ako yung designated SDO? Just like that? And you said okay?

03:18:24.460 --> 03:18:25.240
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir.

03:18:25.360 --> 03:18:26.820
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Wow. No.

03:18:28.750 --> 03:18:37.510
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Under the COA circular, it should only be the head of that agency who happens to be the VP. Or kung ayaw ni VP, mag-designate siya ng

03:18:37.510 --> 03:18:42.350
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: tao na maging SDO niya at meron siyang dokumento pipirman para ini-endorse niya ang SDO na iyon.

03:18:44.680 --> 03:18:54.120
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Who happens to be Paharda? And you said, wala. So sinabi ni Paharda, hello, ako si Paharda, akong designated na SDO ng DepEd. And agad-agad, pininiwalaan niyo.

03:18:55.520 --> 03:19:05.100
Nenita Camposano: During the first encashment, na-mention po ni Ma'am Sonia na mag-e-encash si Mr. Paharda. Pero parang hindi naman yan na-mention na SDO.

03:19:05.100 --> 03:19:10.640
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: No, Ma'am. Ang ibig sabihin dapat, someone should have endorsed Paharda as the SDO for the DepEd.

03:19:12.690 --> 03:19:19.330
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Sabi mo wala. So pumunta lang si Paharda doon, nag-present. Presenta yung sarili niya. Sinabi niya, akong SDO ng Deped. And then sabi niya, okay, sige.

03:19:21.470 --> 03:19:21.910
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: So

03:19:21.910 --> 03:19:24.050
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: hindi kayo sumunod doon sa pata kanan ng Kuwa Circular?

03:19:25.820 --> 03:19:27.720
Nenita Camposano: Wala pong nag-present sa amin, sir.

03:19:27.940 --> 03:19:38.390
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Wala. Okay. So paano naman kung si Paharda talagang authorized na mag-withdraw o magkipag-transact ng limpak-limpak na salapi?

03:19:40.180 --> 03:19:43.760
Nenita Camposano: As pay of the cheque, in honor na po namin yun.

03:19:44.500 --> 03:19:52.840
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: As pay of the cheque. So, sino ang tumatawag sa inyo para sabihin na si Fahada pupunta dyan at mag-withdraw ng such and such amount of money two days before?

03:19:53.660 --> 03:19:55.460
Nenita Camposano: Si Miss Sonia De Leon po.

03:19:55.760 --> 03:19:56.940
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Sino po si Sonia De Leon?

03:19:57.000 --> 03:19:57.200
Nenita Camposano: Siya po

03:19:57.200 --> 03:20:00.280
Nenita Camposano: ang head ng cash division ng DepEd.

03:20:01.260 --> 03:20:05.700
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Okay, siya yung kilala niyong head cash division ng DepEd. Pero, you know what?

03:20:06.180 --> 03:20:08.060
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Nagtataka pa rin ako na...

03:20:08.660 --> 03:20:18.330
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Wala kayong hawak na dokumento na nagsasabing si Fajarda ang designated SDO coming from the head of that agency na

03:20:20.090 --> 03:20:20.630
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: pirmado.

03:20:21.190 --> 03:20:21.870
Nenita Camposano: Wala.

03:20:22.050 --> 03:20:24.980
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Wala, sir. Thank

03:20:24.980 --> 03:20:25.220
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: you,

03:20:25.220 --> 03:20:25.620
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Madam.

03:20:26.360 --> 03:20:27.040
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank

03:20:27.040 --> 03:20:40.580
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: you, Senator Judge Raffi. Actually, the Chair would like to make a brief interjection. The payee of the check is Fajarda. Correct, ma'am?

03:20:40.910 --> 03:20:41.390
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir.

03:20:41.770 --> 03:20:45.490
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: So kung sino, kung kanino nakapangalan yung cheque, doon yung ibibigay.

03:20:46.070 --> 03:20:46.470
Nenita Camposano: Yes.

03:20:46.490 --> 03:20:48.150
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Yung cash o kapalit yung cheque.

03:20:48.850 --> 03:20:49.250
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Kung

03:20:49.250 --> 03:20:57.230
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: SDO man siya o hindi. Pero sa ayon sa COA Circular, SDO lamang ang pwedeng pangalanan ng mga ganyan cheque. Hindi nyo na

03:20:57.230 --> 03:20:58.070
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: po alam yung bagay na yun.

03:20:58.800 --> 03:21:01.000
Nenita Camposano: Nag-ano lang po kami sa pay-in ng cheque, sir.

03:21:01.100 --> 03:21:05.700
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Kung kaninong pangalan yung nakalagay doon, yun po ang sinusunod lang niya. Yes, Representative Chua.

03:21:06.170 --> 03:21:19.310
Rep. Joel R. Chua: Yes, Your Honor. Thank you, Your Honor. Your Honor, the witness has no knowledge as to the designation of Mr. Pajarda and as to the purpose of the fund, Your Honor.

03:21:20.370 --> 03:21:22.350
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: As to being SDO, yes. I believe

03:21:22.350 --> 03:21:23.750
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: you will be presenting another

03:21:23.750 --> 03:21:24.550
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: witness for that.

03:21:24.750 --> 03:21:28.210
Rep. Joel R. Chua: Yes, we are going to present another witness for that, Your Honor. Thank you, Your Honor.

03:21:28.250 --> 03:21:34.030
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Jury noted. Senator Judge Aquino is recognized. You may proceed, sir. When you're ready, you have two minutes. Yes, before my line

03:21:34.030 --> 03:21:40.900
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: of questioning. Gusto ko lang pong klaruhin rin po ma'am, alam niyo po ba na para sa confidential funds yung pondong yan?

03:21:41.440 --> 03:21:42.620
Nenita Camposano: Hindi rin po diba?

03:21:42.720 --> 03:21:44.340
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: And you're not required to ask?

03:21:44.620 --> 03:21:45.640
Nenita Camposano: Yes. Hindi

03:21:45.640 --> 03:21:47.000
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: rin kayo kayo nagtatanong talaga?

03:21:47.160 --> 03:21:47.420
Nenita Camposano: Yes.

03:21:49.280 --> 03:22:03.840
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Pinag-uusapan ko kasi yung covered, suspicious, pati yung salitang unusual. Sa inyo pong pagkakaalam bilang isang bank manager, ano po bang pinagkaya ba ng covered transaction, suspicious transaction?

03:22:05.610 --> 03:22:39.190
Nenita Camposano: Ang covered transaction po is automatic po yung inire-report sa AMLC. May system po ang land bank na ang mga transactions ng banko na in excess of 500,000 ay automatic na naka-report. Ang suspicious transaction naman po ay pagka mayroong kaming nakita kay malaking amount, kay maliit, basta't. Parang doubtful yung transactions. Kailangan po namin i-reporta sa STR.

03:22:39.930 --> 03:22:40.450
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Suspicious

03:22:40.450 --> 03:22:40.910
Nenita Camposano: transaction.

03:22:41.390 --> 03:22:46.110
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Yung covered transaction po, tama po ba na walang human intervention ito? Sa sistema lang po ito?

03:22:46.740 --> 03:22:48.020
Nenita Camposano: The STR?

03:22:48.280 --> 03:22:49.300
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Sa covered transactions.

03:22:49.580 --> 03:22:50.920
Nenita Camposano: May human intervention

03:22:50.920 --> 03:22:51.460
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: po ba ito?

03:22:51.500 --> 03:22:53.980
Nenita Camposano: Wala pong human intervention. System po yan.

03:22:54.240 --> 03:22:59.680
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Ano po ito? Papasok? O palabas? O encashment? O basta kahit anong above 500,000?

03:22:59.680 --> 03:23:04.240
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir. Kahit na ano po above, in excess of 500, nakareport po siya.

03:23:04.320 --> 03:23:07.520
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Okay, so we can safely assume that this transaction was covered.

03:23:09.860 --> 03:23:22.170
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Well, you don't want to deduce that, no? Ayon niyo pong sabihin. Yes. Yung suspicious, sino po nagdedetermine na suspicious ang isang transaction? Who determines that?

03:23:22.710 --> 03:23:30.770
Nenita Camposano: Sa amin po, sa branch, pagka po may napansin kami, ako po ang nagre-report niya.

03:23:31.590 --> 03:23:35.990
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Kayo po, wala hong ibang pwedeng mag-report or ang branch manager lang po yung pwedeng mag-report?

03:23:37.720 --> 03:23:42.960
Nenita Camposano: Ako kasi yung bali nagre-report, ako yung nagsasign ng report.

03:23:43.760 --> 03:23:50.820
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Okay. So, ito po, tinungko rin po ito kanina dun sa manager ng land bank. Pero nais ko lang po marinig rin po sa inyo.

03:23:52.520 --> 03:23:57.240
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Nagkaroon po ba ng suspicious reporting ng transaction ito sa AMLA?

03:24:00.000 --> 03:24:05.580
Nenita Camposano: Hindi po kami pwedeng mag-divulge ng any information regarding sa reporting po ng STR, sir. And

03:24:05.580 --> 03:24:09.600
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: nasa batas naman po yan na hindi po kayo pwedeng mag-divulge.

03:24:09.680 --> 03:24:10.020
Nenita Camposano: Yes.

03:24:10.560 --> 03:24:14.600
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Yung sinabi niyo po kanina, unusual, iba po yun sa suspicious?

03:24:15.200 --> 03:24:15.940
Nenita Camposano: Iba po.

03:24:16.160 --> 03:24:22.460
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Okay. Can you help me understand ano po yung pinagkaiba ng unusual at suspicious sa inyong perspektiba?

03:24:24.040 --> 03:24:28.900
Nenita Camposano: Unusual meaning? Kakaiba lang yung transaction, pero not necessarily suspicious.

03:24:30.020 --> 03:24:39.300
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Yung suspicious po, tama po ba? May exactong definition yan sa mga batas natin? Yung unusual po ay inyo lang pong pakiwari?

03:24:39.340 --> 03:24:40.140
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir.

03:24:40.440 --> 03:24:57.730
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Okay. And kayo po, bilang branch manager, ayaw nyo pong sabihin kung nireport nyo po ito. Pero sa inyo pong karanasan, lahat pong nakikitaan yung hindi pang karaniwan, nireport nyo po ba sa AMLA? Not particularly this case, but in general?

03:24:59.700 --> 03:25:05.120
Nenita Camposano: Hindi naman po. Hindi lahat ng mga unusual transaction ay nire-report namin as suspicious.

03:25:05.520 --> 03:25:05.780
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: All right.

03:25:05.780 --> 03:25:06.960
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chairman.

03:25:09.410 --> 03:25:14.750
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Ejercito is recognized for his interjection. You may proceed, sir. When you're ready, you have two minutes.

03:25:15.190 --> 03:25:36.600
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Yes, thank you, Mr. Providing Judge. Just a clarification. Ma'am, kanina po nakikinig po ako, no? Ang nabanggit niyo, sabi niyo nga. Na ilang beses sabi niya unusual po yung 37.5. Madalas, the transaction sa inyo pong branch ay nag-average 10 to 20 million. Tama ho ba? Ang aking magkakarinig.

03:25:36.800 --> 03:25:38.120
Nenita Camposano: Opo, mga last 10 million.

03:25:38.620 --> 03:25:59.170
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: So sa isang karaniwang araw, ano po yung sa inyo pong experience, ano daw po yung pinakamalaking halaga ng cash na inyo pong nailabas sa inyong sangay para po sa isang client, in this case ito pong ahensya na ang DepEd po? Ano po yung pinakamalaking amount? Ito na po ba yung pinakamalaki? Dahil sabi nyo kanina, unusual.

03:26:01.720 --> 03:26:07.440
Nenita Camposano: Pinakamalaki po ang amount na nailabas nga po ay yung na-encash is yung 37.5.

03:26:08.820 --> 03:26:15.310
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Ito na po. So ito yung nagsimula, kailan po ito nagsimula yung ganitong withdrawals?

03:26:16.470 --> 03:26:18.610
Nenita Camposano: Anong po February, sir?

03:26:20.690 --> 03:26:31.580
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Ito na po, last question. Mr. Presiding Officer, nangyayari po pa ba itong ganitong kalaking amount, ganito kalaking halaga na withdrawal sa ngayon?

03:26:32.320 --> 03:26:38.580
Nenita Camposano: Ay, in my time, wala na po yun. Yun lang po, tatlong yun. Tatlong lang.

03:26:38.740 --> 03:26:39.980
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Well, hindi na po nasundan.

03:26:40.200 --> 03:26:40.940
Nenita Camposano: Wala na po.

03:26:41.300 --> 03:26:41.780
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: That's all.

03:26:41.920 --> 03:26:42.180
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Thank you.

03:26:42.680 --> 03:26:49.340
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Jajercito. If there are no other Senator Judges who wish to make interventions, Chair would like to make a few.

03:26:50.850 --> 03:27:00.120
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Ms. Camposano, ma'am? Tama po bang translation ito? Unusual sa Tagalog, kakaiba. Yes, Your Honor.

03:27:00.140 --> 03:27:02.460
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Suspicious, tama po ba? Kaduda-duda.

03:27:02.880 --> 03:27:03.660
Nenita Camposano: Yes, Your Honor.

03:27:04.380 --> 03:27:26.160
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Sangayon sa AMLOC, yung kaduda-duda dapat i-report, pero yung kakaiba, hindi kailangan i-report. Yes, Your Honor. Tama po. Sabi niyo po kasi kanina, yung unusual, hindi kailangan i-report, pero yung suspicious, kailangan i-report. Sangayon sa batas. Hindi ko po sinasabing suspicious ito. Sinasabi ko lang, yun yung sinasabi ng batas.

03:27:26.640 --> 03:27:43.910
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir. Ang suspicious transaction po ay kailangan natin i-report sa STR, sa AMLC. And yung unusual, kung unusual lang naman siya, wala naman pong suspicious doon sa transaction, hindi po siya kailangan i-report.

03:27:44.510 --> 03:27:52.030
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Isa na lang po katanungan, curious lang po ako. Sabi niyo po, para pangalagaan ang kaligtasan ng inyong empleyado, hindi pwedeng...

03:27:53.240 --> 03:27:53.680
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: ihatid

03:27:53.680 --> 03:28:30.140
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: ng sino mang empleyado ng bangko yung pinagbigyan ng pera, gaano mang kalito, gaano kalaki, dahil kapag kahawak niya na yun, kanya na yun. Tama po ba? Opo. Ibig sabihin po ba nun, pag na-withdraw na yung pera at hawak nun ang depositor yung pera, pag may nang hold up ng bangko, matapos niyang mahawakan yung pera, sa noho yung mawawalan, di na kayo. Ganun po ba yan? Hindi. Sa praktika lang usapan. Gayun din, paglabas niya ng bangko niyo, nahold up siya doon, hawak niya na eh. Wala na kayong pakialam, di ba? Kaya kayo may pulisiyeng gano 'n

03:28:30.140 --> 03:28:39.040
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: na bawal magatid. Dahil nga, pag hawak na niya, kanya na yun. Opo. Kanya na yun, pananagutan niya na yun, wala na kayong pakialam. Ano man ang mangyari doon?

03:28:39.360 --> 03:28:40.020
Nenita Camposano: Yes, Your Honor.

03:28:40.400 --> 03:28:44.040
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Mawala man yun, nakawin man yun, hold upin man yun, labas na kayo doon.

03:28:44.220 --> 03:28:44.820
Nenita Camposano: Yes, Your Honor.

03:28:45.280 --> 03:28:50.240
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: That would be all, Ms. Campuzano. Are there any other interjections or interventions by any of the Senator judges?

03:28:51.790 --> 03:28:53.270
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: One quick question. The

03:28:53.270 --> 03:28:56.550
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senate President is recognized. One quick question, Mr. Presiding Officer.

03:28:56.910 --> 03:29:16.990
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Ms. Camposano, sabi niyo kanina unusual. Pero may nasabi rin kayo kanina in your past experience na may government organization na naglabas ng pera ganang kalaki rin. Bakit unusual po sa DepEd pero hindi unusual dun sa government organization na yun?

03:29:19.210 --> 03:29:39.250
Nenita Camposano: Usually kasi, yung mga ibang agencies po, normal na from naglalabas sila ng ganoon. Ito pong kasing sa DepEd, kaya ko po nasabing unusual is, ito lang pong tatlong to ang nangyari.

03:29:39.630 --> 03:29:45.830
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So in other words, doon sa ibang government agencies, madalas sila ganito kalaking amount ang lumalabas? Regular yun?

03:29:45.970 --> 03:29:46.490
Nenita Camposano: Apo.

03:29:47.030 --> 03:29:48.630
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Sa DepEd, hindi regular?

03:29:49.500 --> 03:29:50.420
Nenita Camposano: Yes, Your Honor. Thank

03:29:50.420 --> 03:29:51.140
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: you, Mr. President.

03:29:52.340 --> 03:29:57.060
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Lacson is recognized for his intervention. You may proceed, sir, when you're ready. Thank

03:29:57.060 --> 03:29:58.260
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: you, Mr. President.

03:30:00.000 --> 03:30:25.450
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: lang. Binabasa ko po yung anti-money laundering act. Wala namang po kaduda-duda nun eh. Either covered or suspicious. Pag covered, may threshold. Maski hindi suspicious, kailangan report. Kung above the threshold amount. Which is 500. Wala po sa batas yung kaduda-duda eh. Either it's suspicious or covered. Transaction.

03:30:29.230 --> 03:30:54.630
Nenita Camposano: Ano kasi yun sir? Pagka ang covered transaction, automatic pong nakareport siya as covered transaction in excess of 500,000. Sa suspicious transaction po, parang nagkaroon po tayo ng doubt, di ba? Then inimbestigahan po natin at yung pong sa investigation natin ay hindi siya pumasa.

03:30:56.670 --> 03:31:01.470
Nenita Camposano: Suspicious pa rin po siya. So that's when kami magre-report a suspicious transaction.

03:31:02.250 --> 03:31:06.990
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Pero there's no such thing in the law na doubtful or kaduda-duda.

03:31:08.700 --> 03:31:13.500
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Unusual. It's just covert or suspicious. So

03:31:13.500 --> 03:31:18.220
Nenita Camposano: parang pinag-nagduda ka and in-investigate.

03:31:18.220 --> 03:31:20.300
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Walang middle layer, ibig sabihin.

03:31:20.620 --> 03:31:21.780
Nenita Camposano: Yes. Pag

03:31:21.780 --> 03:31:40.980
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: above the threshold, tapos covert institution, like casinos, real estate. automatic i-report yun kasi covered institution. Ngayon, ordinary depositor, pumunta sa banko, nag-deposit o nag-withdraw ng more than 500, that's above the threshold. It becomes a covered transaction.

03:31:41.420 --> 03:31:41.800
Nenita Camposano: So

03:31:41.800 --> 03:31:43.320
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: wala akong kaduda-duda.

03:31:45.900 --> 03:32:01.700
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Suspicious. Suspicious lang. Wala yung middle. It's either you categorize it into covered or suspicious. Huwag na ho tayo mag-uusap ng kaduda-duda. Or unusual pala, sorry. Huwag na natin pag-usapan yung unusual.

03:32:03.290 --> 03:32:07.430
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Either kaduda-duda lang or covered. Yes, sir. Thank you.

03:32:11.030 --> 03:32:15.920
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Villanueva for his second round. No,

03:32:16.020 --> 03:32:53.040
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Mr. President. Just a short interjection. I was looking at the BSP circular. number 1215. And in this circular of the Banko Sentral ng Pilipinas, it says here, a transaction is considered unusual when it shows patterns that are inconsistent with the account owner's usual behavior. It's not commensurate with the known business or financial capacity of the account owner or deviates from the account owner's profile. So, naiintindihan nyo po ito when you say unusual, di ba? pumapasok po dito sa BSP Circular.

03:32:56.360 --> 03:33:19.620
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Again, sir? Whenever you said that this is unusual, pumapasok po o dito sa kategoryang ito pumapasok ng BSP Circular 1215, yung binabanggit po ninyo. Ang transaksyon ay considered unusual kung ito po ay nagpapakita ng patterns that are inconsistent with the account owner's usual behavior.

03:33:20.590 --> 03:33:22.770
Nenita Camposano: So kaya po siya unusual, sir? Yun

03:33:22.770 --> 03:33:29.090
Sen. Joel Villanueva: nga po. Kaya tinatanong ko po kayo, whenever you say this, na it's unusual, dahil pumapasok po siya sa kategoryang ito.

03:33:29.190 --> 03:33:29.690
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Yes, sir.

03:33:29.770 --> 03:33:31.210
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Salamat po. Senator

03:33:32.580 --> 03:33:35.380
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Judge Lacson is recognized.

03:33:35.780 --> 03:33:40.940
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Medyo na-confuse lang ako kanina. I did not mean kaduda-duda, but yung unusual na sinasabi kong wala.

03:33:41.540 --> 03:33:42.060
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Thank

03:33:42.540 --> 03:33:48.100
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: you. Kasi yung kaduda-duda na mistook ko as unusual.

03:33:50.410 --> 03:33:55.010
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Ako na po yung nag-translate nun. Suspicious equals kaduda-duda, unusual kakaiba.

03:33:58.680 --> 03:34:02.120
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Lauren Legarde is recognized for her interjection.

03:34:03.080 --> 03:34:03.520
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: You

03:34:03.520 --> 03:34:05.000
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: may proceed, Ma'am Munoz. You have two minutes.

03:34:07.450 --> 03:34:10.070
Sen. Loren Legarda: Just very briefly, thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

03:34:12.140 --> 03:34:38.750
Sen. Loren Legarda: After hearing all the words, unusual, suspicious, illegal, but I just wanted to understand. Ma'am Camposano, matapos po maging subject ng congressional inquiry ang mga transaction na ito, nagsagawa ba ho ang land bank ng anumang internal review kung paano hinanda, na-authorize, or na-release ang cash?

03:34:41.430 --> 03:34:43.010
Nenita Camposano: Internal review po

03:34:43.010 --> 03:34:58.990
Sen. Loren Legarda: ng land bank? Yes. Because you used words unusual, suspicious, all of that. I just wanted to know. Pagkatapos po nangyari yun, was there any internal review? I just wanted to understand that.

03:34:59.670 --> 03:35:01.990
Nenita Camposano: After ng Congress hearing, Your Honor?

03:35:02.270 --> 03:35:07.250
Sen. Loren Legarda: Yes, because doon po namin unang nabatid yung inyong mga statements.

03:35:08.670 --> 03:35:22.910
Nenita Camposano: Hindi ko na po masagot yan, Your Honor, because I was with Land Bank DOTR na po noong time na yun. So kung ano man po yung nangyari with DepEd branch at the time after the Congressional hearing, Hindi ko po alam na.

03:35:23.050 --> 03:35:44.690
Sen. Loren Legarda: So after the hearings, when you made these manifestations, hindi po kayo pamilyar kung nagkaroon po ng pagbabago, ng review, i-assess yung proseso dahil po sa inyong mga kaalaman? Linipat na

03:35:44.690 --> 03:35:45.230
Sen. Loren Legarda: po kayo?

03:35:45.770 --> 03:35:51.380
Nenita Camposano: No. I was with Land Bank, the OTR na, during the congressional hearing.

03:35:51.900 --> 03:35:58.980
Sen. Loren Legarda: Yes. And so, you were not called for any review based on your revelations? Wala

03:35:58.980 --> 03:35:59.240
Sen. Loren Legarda: pa.

03:36:00.260 --> 03:36:55.040
Sen. Loren Legarda: Okay. So, I had many questions. I was supposed to ask you, anong saklaw ng review, ano ang security arrangements, documentation, reporting requirements, but if you're not familiar with the review, so you will not be able to answer. So, do we assume then that the process is still the same? Kung walang binago po, ibig po bang sabihin na land bank considered the existing process sufficient and that the same transaction could still be handled in substantially the same manner today? Gusto ko po lang maintindihan kung unusual, usually... kakausapin dapat yan o a-assess ang proseso. But if it was not, how is the process today? Paano po nagbago kung meron man?

03:36:55.720 --> 03:37:13.940
Nenita Camposano: Kung sa ngayon po, nagbago po ang proseso niyan dahil meron na po tayong BSP guidelines na ang amount lang po ng cash na mailalabas is up to 1 million. Then pagka more than 1 million ay kailangan na po ng necessary approvals.

03:37:13.980 --> 03:37:31.390
Sen. Loren Legarda: Yes, I'm talking about the changes, evaluation, assessment after the congressional inquiry. Are you referring to a BSP guideline that was given after the congressional inquiry?

03:37:31.730 --> 03:37:32.030
Nenita Camposano: Yes,

03:37:32.710 --> 03:38:07.190
Sen. Loren Legarda: that's what I'm referring to. From the time, ma'am, that you gave those statements and if you... found it unusual, and up to now, I wanted to know whether there was any internal, yes, I take note of that, internal assessments to review so that there could be changes for security arrangements. If none, and if not familiar with you, I leave it at that. Except that normally in life, when something is unusual,

03:38:08.780 --> 03:38:26.920
Sen. Loren Legarda: which is not necessarily suspicious, which is not necessarily illegal, but you assess and you make changes to improve the process. But you're saying you are not familiar with any such investigations or assessment or review.

03:38:28.080 --> 03:38:29.520
Nenita Camposano: Yes, ma'am. Okay.

03:38:29.600 --> 03:38:30.000
Sen. Loren Legarda: Thank

03:38:30.000 --> 03:38:44.900
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: you. Thank you, ma'am. Senator Judge Padilla first. Apologies, Senator Allen. Senator Judge Padilla, for his interjections thereafter, Senator Judge Alan Cayetano. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed with your ready. Maraming salamat po. Isang mabilis lang

03:38:44.900 --> 03:38:50.420
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: po ito. Pagka sinabi pong unusual, hindi pangkaraniwan. Hindi po ba?

03:38:50.820 --> 03:38:51.420
Nenita Camposano: Yes, sir.

03:38:51.460 --> 03:38:54.940
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: Kapag sinabing suspicious, ibig sabihin kahinahinala.

03:38:55.280 --> 03:38:55.980
Nenita Camposano: Apo, sir.

03:38:56.100 --> 03:38:58.920
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: Wala po kayong nakitang kahinahinala, hindi po ba?

03:38:59.440 --> 03:39:00.400
Nenita Camposano: Wala naman po.

03:39:00.460 --> 03:39:01.960
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: Ibig sabihin hindi po illegal.

03:39:04.220 --> 03:39:07.970
Nenita Camposano: Wala naman. Ang ano lang po kasi namin is yun sa... Check and cash.

03:39:08.230 --> 03:39:12.990
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: Ibig sabihin wala pong illegal. Maraming salamat po sa prosecution naman po ako.

03:39:14.810 --> 03:39:19.570
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: Ginong prosecutor, pangkaraniwan po ba ang confidential fund?

03:39:22.380 --> 03:39:30.200
Rep. Joel R. Chua: Your Honor, yung confidential fund po, sa aking pagkakaalam, ito po'y binibigay. Pangkaraniwan po ba siya na

03:39:30.200 --> 03:39:30.760
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: ibinibigay?

03:39:30.860 --> 03:39:34.540
Rep. Joel R. Chua: Depende po. Depende po sa mga government agency at saka

03:39:34.540 --> 03:39:34.740
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: head ng agency.

03:39:34.760 --> 03:39:38.240
Sen. Robinhood “Robin” Padilla: So hindi po siya pangkaraniwan kasi depende? Tama po. Salamat po.

03:39:39.020 --> 03:39:46.280
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Padilla. Senator Judge Alan Cayetano is recognized for his interjections. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

03:39:47.520 --> 03:39:48.060
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: I

03:39:48.060 --> 03:39:53.740
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: think most senators already clarified, but just a little bit more. Magandang hapon, Madam Witness.

03:39:54.760 --> 03:39:55.320
Nenita Camposano: So,

03:39:55.700 --> 03:40:00.360
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: are you familiar with confidential or intelligence or discretionary funds?

03:40:00.760 --> 03:40:01.340
Nenita Camposano: No, sir.

03:40:01.480 --> 03:40:22.110
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: So, yung usual or unusual? Depende kung saan ka naka-assign. Kasi for example, kung sa Malacanang ka naka-assign, and parating may intelligence funds ang Malacanang, and whether, I don't know how much they usually withdraw, whether it's 25, 50, 100. So if they always do it, then it's usual, right?

03:40:22.350 --> 03:40:23.250
Nenita Camposano: Yes. If

03:40:23.250 --> 03:40:34.450
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: it's just a one time that year, or unusual, bakit suddenly, right? So whether it's you or the previous witness, ang tinatanong lang namin kung usual sa branch niya.

03:40:36.810 --> 03:40:57.370
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: In your case kasi you've been assigned to different branches handling different agencies but not all agencies have confidential funds. So yung pag tinanong sa'yo usual, you're just being honest kung again, if it's usual or not usual or unusual, right?

03:40:57.870 --> 03:40:58.650
Nenita Camposano: Put it

03:40:58.650 --> 03:41:02.530
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: another way, diba? If you're a kind of person that you love everyone,

03:41:04.450 --> 03:41:56.980
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: and then first time ko pumunta sa branch mo, I love Alan, then it's usual. Sabi nga ni Tom Jones, it's not unusual to be loved by you. Kung yun yung usual. If you're the type of person naman that you don't like anyone, then suddenly I go to your branch, sasabihin naman ng mga tao doon, Ma'am, medyo unusual. Ba't mo nagustuhan siya? So I think yun din yung isang thing na-clarify ni Sen. Tulfo, ni Sen. Lakson, etc. na iba yung suspicious and covert kasi may legal implications yun. Yung useful, unusual. We're just trying to get to the truth of what's happening here. So the other point what I want to make is that siguro sa prosecution ko na ito itanong dahil we're all legislators here, Honorable Chua. Is it useful for DepEd to have confidential funds?

03:41:57.690 --> 03:42:02.850
Rep. Joel R. Chua: Your Honor, I believe that this is the first time that DepEd received confidential money.

03:42:02.850 --> 03:42:03.130
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Yes, in

03:42:03.130 --> 03:43:05.280
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: fact, here in the Senate, in COCUS, ako lang halos ang nag-object. I think dalawa lang kami o tatlo. Ang sinabi ko nun sa chairman namin ng Committee on Finance, if the Vice President needs that amount, let's put it all in OVP. Same amount na nire-request niya kasi at least dun usually naman talaga meron kasi nga or pwede. Kasi vice president siya. And then kung siya ay nasa security council or kung siya ay nasa any law enforcement. Ang argument ko nun, if you put it in DepEd, paano pag napalitan yung sekretary, will we continue it, etc. So anyway, I just agree with the other senators here that as we go along, let's help the public understand the difference between covered, suspicious, and... usual, unusual. Para lang walang conclusions that are made that are prejudicial to either the prosecution or the defense. Thank you. Thank you, Senator

03:43:05.280 --> 03:43:06.180
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Judge Cayetano.

03:43:08.350 --> 03:43:26.390
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: There being no other senator judges who wish to make interjections, Ms. Camposano, you are excused, ma'am. Thank you very much for your time and your cooperation. Salamat po sa inyong pagkikilahok. sa pagdinig na ito ng impeachment court. Your excuse, ma'am.

03:43:29.010 --> 03:43:36.410
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: On the part of the prosecution, may I know who are your witnesses for next week's trial?

03:43:37.550 --> 03:43:38.510
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: The lead

03:43:38.510 --> 03:43:39.610
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: prosecutor is recognized.

03:43:40.250 --> 03:44:43.290
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, and in response to your question, we are requesting for the issuance of Sabina Ducez-Tecum and Sabina A. Testificant for the following witnesses. One, Roderick C. Wamil. Former State Auditor of COA ICFAO. Address is Commission and Audit, Central Office Compound, Commonwealth Avenue, Quezon City. 2. Ms. Sylene May L. Del Campo. Present State Auditor of COA ICFAO with same address. 3. Ms. Marivic Pareja. Director of House of Representative, Legislative Information, Resources Management Department, Batasan Pambansa Complex, Batasan Hills, Quezon City. Your Honor, these three witnesses are intended to be presented on August 3, August 4, and August 5, trial schedules.

03:44:43.710 --> 03:44:44.410
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: In that order,

03:44:44.590 --> 03:44:46.070
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Honorable

03:44:46.070 --> 03:44:50.750
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Bistro. So first, Roderick, next, Cylene, and third would be Maravick.

03:44:51.260 --> 03:44:52.260
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: That's correct, Your Honor.

03:44:52.480 --> 03:45:04.800
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: The Clerk of Court is directed to issue the corresponding subpoena at testificandum, subpoena dosis tecum to the aforementioned witnesses at the aforestated addresses of the witnesses mentioned by the lead prosecutor. So, ordered.

03:45:08.370 --> 03:45:11.630
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Chair would like to dispose of one other administrative matter.

03:45:13.460 --> 03:46:32.900
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Last July 15, the Honorable Aquino asked a question before this Court regarding the procedure. If after each article we will hear both the prosecution and the defense and the presiding officer responded in the negative, citing as basis the precedent in the Corona impeachment trial, the only trial that actually went through the whole course, wherein the prosecution finished presentation of their evidence with respect to all of the articles of impeachment that they did not withdraw. Thereafter, the defense presented their evidence with respect to the articles of impeachment that were not withdrawn by the prosecution. Sometime last week, the presiding officer, based on some of the suggestions by some of the senator judges, called for a sidebar with the lead prosecutor and the lead counsel for respondent to throw a question at them if they're open to changing the procedure. to the one suggested in open court by Senator Bam Aquino. However, subject to one condition, that both parties should be agreeable, that both parties should agree. We are in receipt of a manifestation. Actually, just a reminder to the Council, to the panel of prosecutors, you filed a manifestation, not a manifestation.

03:46:35.570 --> 03:47:27.640
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: The manifestation dated 7-27, and the response of the respondents dated 7-28. wherein it is clear based on your written manifestations that there is no agreement between the two parties. Therefore, we shall proceed as originally ruled by the Chair from the inquiry of Senator Bam Aquino. We shall finish with the presentation of the evidence in chief of the prosecutors for all the articles of impeachment that they will not withdraw. I'm saying that only because of the corona impeachment experience we had wherein some articles were withdrawn by the prosecution. Thereafter, we will hear the evidence in chief of the respondent for all the articles that remain or all the articles that evidence will be presented by the prosecution. So ordered. If there are no other matters, Senator Judge Zubiri is recognized.

03:47:34.430 --> 03:48:26.940
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” Zubiri: Mr. President, Mr. Presiding Officer. There is just a request from most of our colleagues here that if we can adjust our schedule in the mornings to 10.30 in the morning till 3.30 in the afternoon. Because like the minority leader who comes from Bicutan, inaabutan po siya ng traffic pag maaga. Ganun din ang haba ng biyahe niya. So baka pwede naman ma-adjust natin ng 10.30 ng umaga. At then 3.30 ng hapon tayo matapos. At 4 o'clock tayo mag-session. Kasi anyway, ililipat lang naman natin yung mga lamesa. Madali naman yan gawin. You don't need one hour to... That is the first question. I have a second question. The second question is, may we start our legislative session today earlier? We will respond to both. Thank you, Mr. President. Senator

03:48:26.940 --> 03:48:37.150
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Lapid would like to amend that a bit. If we can start at 10.30 and end at 2.30 so that we can begin our session regularly at 3.00.

03:48:39.620 --> 03:48:41.000
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge

03:48:41.000 --> 03:48:47.960
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Mr. Senate President, Mr. Presiding Officer, i-caucus na lang po natin yung first manifestation ni Majority Leader.

03:48:47.960 --> 03:48:54.920
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: So if you will hold the caucus first, we have to adjourn today at a specific time. So will it be 10:00 or 10:30?

03:48:54.920 --> 03:48:58.690
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: I would prefer 10.00 o'clock so 
I would suggest na ikokus natin.

03:48:58.690 --> 03:49:02.450
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: 10.00 for this Monday, August 3. Then we adjust after the caucus.

03:49:04.730 --> 03:49:13.230
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: But for this afternoon, upon the authorization of the Senate President, we shall convene at 3pm, the regular session of the Senate for today.

03:49:15.500 --> 03:49:35.140
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: There being no other matters to be taken up, the trial is adjourned until August 3 at 10am in the morning and session for this afternoon shall be convened. At 3pm for the information of all the senators. Trial is adjourned.
